    "title": "Dua Lipa to Margaret Cho: What's happening on Wednesday? - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Knx News 97 1 Fm ,\n16 hours ago\nMidweek in Los Angeles is stacked from stadium soccer and global pop stars to alt-pop shows and sharp-tongued stand-up comedy.\nQuinn XCII – LOOK! I’m Alive Tour\nDate/Time: Wednesday, Oct. 8, 2025 · 7:00 PM – 9:00 PM\nPlace: Hollywood Palladium, 6215 W. Sunset Blvd., Los Angeles, CA 90028\nPop and alt favorite Quinn XCII (pronounced Ninety-Two ) brings his seventh studio album LOOK! I’m Alive to the Hollywood Palladium. Known for Platinum singles like “Straightjacket” and “Love Me Less,” Gold-certified hits including “Stay Next To Me” and “Always Been You,” and collaborations with Noah Kahan, AJR, and Chelsea Cutler, Quinn delivers a genre-blending mix of pop, alternative, and folk-inspired sounds with an unmistakable charm. Expect a high-energy show and plenty of fan favorites.\nFull Link: Quinn XCII Tickets\nAngel City FC vs. Toronto\nDate/Time: Wednesday, Oct. 8, 2025 · 7:30 PM – 9:30 PM\nPlace: BMO Stadium, 3939 S. Figueroa St., Los Angeles, CA 90037\nAngel City FC faces off against Toronto in a midweek home match at BMO Stadium. With a passionate fan base and high-energy play, it’s always an electric night for professional women’s soccer in Los Angeles.\nFull Link: Angel City FC Tickets\nDua Lipa – Radical Optimism Tour\nDate/Time: Wednesday, Oct. 8, 2025 · 7:30 PM – 9:30 PM\nPlace: Kia Forum, 3900 W. Manchester Blvd., Inglewood, CA 90305\nGlobal pop star Dua Lipa brings her Radical Optimism Tour to the Kia Forum for her Los Angeles finale. Known for hits like “Levitating” and “Don’t Start Now,” Dua closes out her tour with a high-energy, dance-heavy performance.\nFull Link: Dua Lipa Tickets\nMargaret Cho – Stand-Up at Largo\nDate/Time: Wednesday, Oct. 8, 2025 · 8:00 PM – 10:00 PM\nPlace: Largo at the Coronet, 366 N. La Cienega Blvd., Los Angeles, CA 90048\nComedy trailblazer Margaret Cho brings her fearless, socially aware brand of stand-up to Largo. With Grammy-nominated comedy albums, Broadway credits, and iconic TV roles under her belt, Cho’s sharp wit, bold commentary, and cultural critiques have made her a legend in the comedy world. Expect a sold-out show full of laughter and thought-provoking moments.\nFull Link: Margaret Cho Tour Info\nF ollow KNX News 97.1 FM\nTwitter | Facebook | Instagram | TikTok",
